Title: "Overview"
Id: "47336735-cb72-43c0-85a4-be6c2239485d"

Text: "A structural group may have a bracketed heading.

```mlg-fragment
[\set]
Declares: X

[theorem.ordinal.trichotomy]
Theorem:
then: ...
```

The group kind determines which heading parser is used:

- **command** headings, required on `Declares:`, `Defines:`, `Realizes:`, `Refines:`,
  `States:`, and `Equivalent:`, and optional on `Axiom:`, `Theorem:`, and
  `Conjecture:`
- **label** headings, optional on alias items, `Requires:`/`Enables:` items,
  documented items, specify items, and clause groups — and required on the
  `have:`/`asserting:` items of a `Justification:` section
- **author** headings for `Person:`
- **resource** headings for `Resource:`
- **topic** headings for `Topic:`

`Disambiguates:` takes an operator or function form as its heading, and
`Relation:`, `Specify:`, and the prose and `Text…:` groups take no heading.

Infix-specification headings (`\:...:/`) are allowed only on `Declares:`, and
refined headings (`::`) only on `Refines:`.

A heading is never what determines the structural group kind. The first section
label does that."
Id: "77b36fee-6c6d-47c9-a0da-f0e040408850"
